  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"4.1.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: stepup\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/s/stepup/stepup-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 317bb40c09f9e3ef0a4267a3d264d6086c064bce0f00c522856c0ea524e6b434\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - stepup = stepup.core.__main__:main\n      - sb = stepup.core.__main__:sb_main\n      - sc-render-jinja = stepup.core.render_jinja:main\n\n# Notes on the dependencies:\n# The file watcher of StepUp uses a platform-specific backend,\n# so there is one noarch build per OS, distinguished by a virtual package:\n# - Linux: asyncinotify (watchfiles is an optional alternative,\n#   selected with STEPUP_WATCHER=watchfiles).\n# - macOS and Windows: watchfiles.\n# These dependencies are not made optional because they add major value.\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - setuptools >=77.0\n    - setuptools-scm >=8.1\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - if: linux\n      then:\n        - __linux\n        - asyncinotify >=4.0.9\n    - if: osx\n      then:\n        - __osx\n        - watchfiles >=1.3.0\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - __win\n        - watchfiles >=1.3.0\n    - attrs >=23.1.0\n    - cattrs >=23.2.3\n    - jinja2 >=3.1.6\n    - parse >=1.19.1\n    - path >=16.14.0\n    - pyyaml >=6.0\n    - rich >=13.0.0\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - stepup.core\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - script:\n      - stepup --help\n      - sb --help\n      - sc-render-jinja --help\n\nabout:\n  summary: A dynamic Python build tool for reproducible workflows\n  description: |\n    StepUp is a dynamic build tool and a modern alternative to Make.\n    Its defining feature is that workflow generation and execution are unified:\n    a plan.py script defines the initial build steps.\n    While the workflow is being executed, any step can add more steps and\n    dependencies, based on the outputs built so far.\n    This makes StepUp ideal for builds where the full set of dependencies\n    cannot be determined in advance.\n\n    StepUp Core provides the basic framework for StepUp,\n    without any domain-specific features.\n  license: LGPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - LICENSES/LicenseRef-StepUp-Logo-v1.txt\n  homepage: https://reproducible-reporting.github.io/stepup-core/\n  repository: https://github.com/reproducible-reporting/stepup-core/\n  documentation: https://reproducible-reporting.github.io/stepup-core/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - tovrstra\n",
